---
import TimerPage from '@/layouts/TimerPage.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import { faqs } from '@/data/faqs';
import { relatedTimers, relatedPosts } from '@/data/related';
import { defaultConfigs } from '@/engine/presets';
import { tabatas } from '@/data/tabatas';
---

<TimerPage
  title="Tabata Timer – Free 20/10 x 8 Timer with Beeps"
  description="Free Tabata timer preset to 20 seconds work, 10 seconds rest, 8 rounds. Editable, with distinct work and rest beeps, screen wake lock and no login."
  path="/tabata"
  h1="Tabata timer"
  lede="20 seconds on, 10 seconds off, 8 rounds, 4 minutes. Preset to the original protocol and editable."
  config={defaultConfigs.tabata}
  faq={faqs['/tabata']}
  related={relatedTimers['/tabata']!}
  posts={relatedPosts['/tabata']}
  crumbName="Tabata timer"
>
  <Section num="01" title="The protocol" flush>
    <p>
      Izumi Tabata's 1996 study had speed skaters do 20 seconds at 170 percent of VO2 max, 10
      seconds rest, eight times. Four minutes. It improved both aerobic and anaerobic capacity,
      which is why the name stuck. The catch is the intensity: if you can talk during the 20 seconds
      you are not doing Tabata, you are doing intervals with a Tabata timer. Both are fine.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section num="02" title="Common variants">
    <ul>
      {tabatas.map((t) => (
        <li>
          <a href={t.path}>{t.h1}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>Or edit the numbers under the timer. The last setup you used is remembered.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section num="03" title="Sounds">
    <p>
      A 10 second get-ready count, then a rising pair for work, a falling pair for rest, ticks for
      the last three seconds of each, and a three-note finish. The digits change colour too, for
      when the music is loud.
    </p>
  </Section>
</TimerPage>
